[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

; Package 8 B2 - the production Fighter Mode HUD, rebuilt by UR-HUDF (pulp UI
; redesign, HUD-F2 "top versus bars") and restyled by TG-HUDF (Temporal Glass,
; UI_SPEC_GLASS 3.4, 4.5).
;
; Attached by FighterSimulationDriver for every stage rather than authored into
; each stage scene. The kit's top shade (fighter_top_shade.tres) sits behind the
; band; both clusters hang from the TOP corners (36 / 22 screen px: FighterHUD.cs
; keeps the corners pinned at every UI scale), the glass timer plate
; (GlassPanelTimer) hangs from the top centre, and a lens row per player (three
; 54 px lenses plus the two status badges) hangs below each cluster. The glass
; widgets (portrait frame, slot shape, stock stars, block pips, Defy icon, lenses,
; badges, the HP and Ultimate tubes over their ProgressBar value carriers) are
; built by FighterHUD.cs because they are code-drawn and the stock / shield counts
; are data-driven. TopRow is a plain Control: FighterHUD.cs lays out the slot
; shape, the name (shrunk to fit) and the P tag on its 30 px row.
;
; The old Label glyph nodes (SlotBadge, the Damage / Control status indicators,
; DefySeal, the three cooldown icons with their Radial) are kept under their old
; paths as accessibility and test carriers, hidden: tests and tooltips read their
; Text, and shape now rides the icons. P2 HP and meter fill from the outer edge
; (fill_mode = 1), which also mirrors their glass tubes (R6).

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/UI/FighterHUD.cs" id="1_hud"]
